@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# Saltlord's Remix 1.1.0 implementation report
+
+Status: source implementation complete; GitHub compilation and device regression pass pending.
+
+## Implemented
+
+- HD cinematic orientation independent from gameplay, including the landscape preference,
+  an in-player Rotate control and restoration of the prior gameplay orientation.
+- HUD Toggle added to the default KH Remix touch set and migrated into older saved Remix
+  layouts without resetting existing controls.
+- Four aspect-aware fresh-install KH defaults based on the supplied references: cover
+  portrait, cover landscape, unfolded portrait and unfolded landscape.
+- Context-sensitive eligibility kept separate from manual visibility and auto-hidden state.
+- Controller suppression retained across context changes; disconnect restores eligible
+  controls without requiring a settings toggle cycle.
+- Existing saved layout identity and data retained across updates.
+- Automatic, Portrait 4:3, Landscape 4:3 and Landscape Fullscreen launch profiles.
+  The retired experimental forced-Flex value migrates to Automatic.
+- Landscape Fullscreen uses the whole safe viewport instead of a fixed 16:9 cap.
+- One-time fresh-install welcome, reopenable Remix Guide, verified feature list, known
+  limitations, credits, AI-assistance disclosure and traceable version/commit information.
+- Public identity changed to `Melon Mix: Saltlord's Remix` without changing the established
+  `com.nireves333.melonmix.adaptivekh` Remix installation identity.
+- Remix 1.1.0 / version code 1010 on the existing update line.
+- Approved launcher, adaptive foreground, monochrome themed icon and splash assets.
+- Oxblood, near-black, warm-white and restrained gold application palette.
+- Source-based README and Remix feature/change audit.
+- One consolidated app patch plus one native-core delta and one clearly named build workflow.
+
+## Removed or deliberately not added
+
+- The experimental forced-Flex launch profile is not exposed. Automatic remains the only
+  profile that responds to fold/tabletop posture.
+- Portrait Widescreen was evaluated and rejected because it did not provide a distinct,
+  proportionally sound use case beyond Portrait 4:3 and Automatic.
+- The stale forced-frame Re:Coded white-screen workaround was removed. The reported white
+  screen was caused by a corrupted ROM dump and is not listed as a Remix defect.
+- Texture-toggle and Open Settings plugin actions were not added to the default touch layout:
+  the former needs a deliberate UX/icon decision and the latter duplicates existing UI.
+
+## Remaining known limitations
+
+- A live orientation/posture change in Automatic can leave native 3D projection distorted
