+# Saltlord's Remix major-build audit
+
+Status: implementation in progress. This document records source-confirmed behaviour; device-only items remain explicitly marked for playtesting.
+
+## Baseline
+
+- Stable functional baseline: the Saltlord's Remix 1.0.8 patch chain through v30.
+- Android package identity remains `com.nireves333.melonmix` plus the existing adaptive Remix debug suffix used by the release workflow.
+- No package/application ID migration is planned for this build.
+- Re:Coded's previous white-screen report was caused by a corrupted ROM dump and is not treated as a Remix defect.
+
+## Confirmed Remix differences from stock Android MelonMix
+
+### Kingdom Hearts touch controls
+
+- Editable `KHDS: TOUCH REMIX` layout configuration.
+- Relative movement touch zone and relative camera stick/swipe zone.
+- KH command pad.
+- Dedicated touch actions for Attack/Confirm, Jump/Cancel, Guard/Ability and X/Deck Command.
+- Lock-On, L/Shortcut hold toggle, Map/Navi, HUD toggle and manual touch-control hide.
+- Per-control alpha, position and scale through the layout model/editor.
+- Grid snapping in the layout editor.
+
+### Visibility and input behaviour
+
+- Context-sensitive control eligibility driven by native game-scene events for Days and Re:Coded.
+- Configurable timed auto-hide.
+- Physical-controller-aware touch visibility.
+- This major build separates scene eligibility from manual visibility, auto-hidden state and controller suppression so a scene change cannot resurrect hidden controls.
+
+### Display and foldable handling
+
+- Per-game launch profiles: Automatic, Portrait 4:3, Landscape 4:3 and Landscape Fullscreen.
+- Adjustable portrait screen position.
+- Full safe-width landscape output, including ultra-wide displays.
+- Automatic fold/posture-aware layout selection and tabletop presentation.
+- Known limitation: a live posture/orientation change can leave the native 3D projection stretched until restart.
+- Known limitation: HD cinematics are not constrained to the tabletop upper panel.
+
+### HD cinematics
+
+- External HD cinematic playback with subtitles and pause-menu overlay integration.
+- This major build adds a preference for temporary landscape cinematic orientation.
+- This major build adds an in-cinematic Rotate control and restores the exact gameplay orientation afterward.
+
+### Presentation and identity
+
+- Adaptive KH backgrounds and KH-styled pause/menu presentation.
+- Saltlord's Remix title/subtitle treatment.
+- This major build changes the public label to `Melon Mix: Saltlord's Remix`.
+- This major build introduces a restrained red/black/warm-gold application palette.
+- This major build adds one-time fresh-install onboarding plus a manually reopenable Remix guide.
+
+## Control audit
+
+Source comparison between Android `Input`, layout components and the Days/Re:Coded plugin mappings found two plugin actions not exposed as dedicated Remix touchscreen components:
+
+- `Toggle Replacement Textures`: potentially useful, but currently omitted pending a deliberate UX/icon decision; adding it merely for completeness would clutter the default layout.
+- `Open Settings`: intentionally omitted as redundant with the emulator's existing settings/navigation UI.
+
+All other useful game-specific mappings are represented by a touch component or by a dedicated combined control.
+
+## Portrait widescreen evaluation
+
+No dedicated Portrait Widescreen profile is planned. The existing Portrait 4:3 profile already maximises a proportionally correct DS/KH viewport within portrait bounds. A portrait-fullscreen profile would either create an unusually narrow native projection or encourage distortion while duplicating Automatic behaviour. This does not solve a distinct use case strongly enough to justify another launch option.
+
+## Update and layout persistence
+
+- Saved layouts are loaded from the existing `layouts.json` identity and are not replaced by the current bundled default.
+- Fresh installs receive the newest KH Remix seed.
+- This major build introduces a component-schema migration: the HUD toggle is appended to older saved KH Remix layouts without changing existing coordinates, scales, alpha values or other components.
+- The fresh-install KH Remix seed now uses four aspect-aware presets derived from
+  Dom's canonical play-tested references: cover portrait, cover landscape,
+  unfolded portrait and unfolded landscape.
+
+## Branding assets
+
+The approved Saltlord's Remix icon has been installed across:
+
+- legacy launcher icons in every `mipmap-*` density;
+- adaptive `mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml`;
+- adaptive foreground resources in every density;
+- adaptive background colour;
+- monochrome launcher drawable;
+- splash artwork used by the splash theme and ROM-shortcut fallback.
+
+The adaptive foreground stays inside Android's safe region; legacy launcher,
+monochrome themed-icon and splash variants are generated from the same master mark.
+
+## Device-side regression testing still required
+
+- Days and verified-good Re:Coded boot/gameplay.
+- Scene transitions while auto-hidden.
+- Controller connect/disconnect across scene transitions.
+- Cinematic landscape preference, manual rotation, pause/skip and restoration into each gameplay profile.
+- Existing customised layout after update and fresh-install default layout.
+- Cover, unfolded inner and tabletop states on the Fold.
+- Launcher label/icon and onboarding persistence.
